@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+---
+"@gpuix/native": minor
+"@gpuix/solid": patch
+---
+
+Support independent macOS renderer windows in one embedded GPUI application.
+Scope paint, selection, search, automation and scrolling caches by GPUI window
+identity; fence closed-window and replaced-root callback delivery. Add explicit
+window close/liveness/identity/title methods. Keep the macOS application available
+after its last window closes so the host can open another renderer or exit after
+tick returns false. Other platform lifecycle policies are unchanged.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 78d02ef..e7813df 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -32,6 +32,60 @@ absolute canonical path before importing `@gpuix/native`. Application bindings
 must load that same file. Loading a second addon creates separate native state.
 This extension API does not add multi-window support.
 
+## Multiple native windows on macOS
+
+Create one `GpuixRenderer` per window and call `init` on each. They share one
+embedded GPUI application, platform and event pump on the macOS main thread.
+Each renderer owns its GPUI window handle, tree, focus, input state, scrolling,
+selection, paint/automation bounds and search ordinals. Element IDs are local
+to a renderer: two windows may both contain element `1`.
+
+For Solid, use `createRoot(renderer)` for each independent reactive tree. The
+convenience `render()` function remains a single-window hot-reload slot.
+
+```tsx
+import { createRoot, createRenderer } from '@gpuix/solid'
+
+const left = createRenderer()
+const right = createRenderer()
+left.init({ title: 'Left' })
+right.init({ title: 'Right' })
+const leftRoot = createRoot(left)
+const rightRoot = createRoot(right)
+leftRoot.render(() => <text>Left window</text>)
+rightRoot.render(() => <text>Right window</text>)
+// One host timer is enough: tick on either initialized renderer pumps all windows.
+const timer = setInterval(() => {
+  if (!left.tick()) clearInterval(timer)
+}, 8)
+```
+
+The following methods are macOS-only:
+
+- `isWindowOpen(): boolean`: false before initialization and after native close.
+- `closeWindow(): void`: close only this renderer's window and release its native
+  state. Further native window operations reject. Create a new renderer to reopen.
+- `getWindowId(): string`: opaque GPUI generation-bearing identity, not an element ID.
+- `getWindowTitle(): string`: actual native title after the most recent render.
+
+`tick()` returns false when no windows remain; it does not terminate the JS host.
+The application uses GPUI's normal macOS explicit-quit policy, so a fresh renderer
+may open a window even after the last one closed. Resume the host timer then.
+Quit/cmd-q still explicitly quits the application. The first initialized window
+chooses the application menu name. Close/minimize/zoom actions target the window
+whose GPUI action context received them.
+
+`createRendererState` fences event delivery after native close and rechecks root
+ownership when a scheduled callback runs. Solid roots may safely `unmount()`
+after their native window closes; pending mutations are discarded. Hosts that
+construct `GpuixRenderer` with a raw callback must dispatch through this shared
+root state (or check `isWindowOpen()` themselves): napi callbacks already queued
+at close can still reach that raw callback. Dispose the closed Solid root to
+release its JavaScript computations.
+
+Other platforms retain their existing single-window lifecycle and are not
+qualified for this macOS multi-window API.
+
 ## Quickstart
 
 Create an app from the official example. The command downloads only
